{
  "title": "SaaS Boilerplate \u2014 saas (7,102\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: SaaS Boilerplate\nDomain: saas | Scale: medium | Stars: 7,102\nProblem: Provides a production-ready, fully-featured foundation for building SaaS applications with minimal effort. Solves the problem of repetitive SaaS infrastructure setup by bundling authentication, multi-tenancy, RBAC, and deployment tooling.\nTarget users: SaaS founders and startup developers, Full-stack engineers building commercial applications, Teams needing rapid SaaS deployment\nCore features: Authentication & User Management; Multi-tenancy with Team Support; Role-Based Access Control & Permissions; User Impersonation; Internationalization (i18n); Error Reporting & Logging; E2E Testing & CI/CD Pipeline; Landing Page & Dashboard UI\nIntegrations: Clerk (authentication & user management), Sentry (error reporting), Drizzle ORM (database management), PostgreSQL / SQLite / MySQL (databases), GitHub Actions (CI/CD), Playwright (E2E testing), Spotlight (debugging), Crowdin (internationalization), Arcjet (security)\nTech stack: Next.js 14 + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Shadcn UI + Radix UI + Next.js API Routes + TypeScript + PostgreSQL / SQLite / MySQL via Drizzle ORM + Next.js standalone + GitHub Actions + Sentry\nKey libraries: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI, Clerk, Drizzle ORM, React Hook Form, TanStack React Table, Next-intl, Next-themes, Pino, Vitest, Playwright, Storybook\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Full-stack monolithic architecture with Next.js App Router maximizes developer velocity for SaaS startups while maintaining type safety via TypeScript across frontend and backend.\n- Composition of battle-tested third-party services (Clerk for auth, Drizzle for ORM, Sentry for observability) reduces custom complexity and accelerates time-to-market.\n- Comprehensive testing pyramid (unit tests with Vitest, component tests with React Testing Library, E2E with Playwright) and CI/CD automation provide confidence for rapid iteration.\n- Multi-tenancy baked into foundational architecture and UI component library (Shadcn) enables straightforward customization for diverse customer needs without rearchitecting.",
